  "id": "ganda_baja_dalkhai",
  "name": "Ganda baja and dalkhai (western Odisha folk ensemble)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ganda baja, also called dulduli baja, is the folk band of western Odisha, played at weddings, festivals and dances by musicians of the Ganda community on the dhol, the large nisan kettledrum, the tasa and the double-reed mahuri. It accompanies dalkhai, the song-dance young women perform around Dussehra in honour of the goddess Dalkhai. Here the nagara card stands in for the nisan and the mukhavina card, a small double-reed pipe, for the mahuri.",
  "recipe": "classic modern ganda baja and dalkhai, carnival Processional, south Asian branch. group vocals. dhol, nagara indian, tasha, mukhavina. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
